<title>BELGIUM: EU probes Tyco/ADT, Mannesmann/Valourec deals.</title>
<headline>EU probes Tyco/ADT, Mannesmann/Valourec deals.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it was opening a routine probe into the following corporate agreements under the European Union's merger rules, which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions:</p>
<p>-- U.S.'s Tyco International proposed control of Bermuda-based electronics security firm ADT Ltd. (Notified on April 25)</p>
<p>-- Mannesmann's Mannesmannroehren-Werke proposed control of the whole of Vallourec. (Notified on April 25)</p>
<p>The Commission has about a month to approve the deals or start a full probe.</p>
</text>
